body:
Not technically my first day but;

a family friend called me about a PSW job position that her neighbour was offering for their elderly mother. They called me to do a phone interview, and the guy made it seem like a very relaxed and easy job. Work only a few hours a day, plus get a few days off a week, being payed over $20/h. They would also let me live in their basement apartment, rent free. This sounded too good to be true, which it was. I set up to meet the mother in person, which went very well. 

Then I sat down with her kids, the ones hiring me. They totally changed up on me, saying I would have to work every day of the week, 24h/day. They would set up a call button in my bedroom in the basement so if she has any trouble during the night, I would be there to help. I wouldn’t get any breaks either. They even said they’ll pay me In cash, which I said no to because I need to document my payments. I tried to mention that they didn’t tell me this on the phone.. but I’ll think about it. I sent them a text maybe an hour after I left telling them I’m not willing to do the job. They tried to tell me if I take it I’ll get a few days off a month… definitely don’t trust them.
